nodecode-birkin is a rewrite of ashmoonori-afk's ashmoonori-afk/birkin-mnemosyne:

https://github.com/ashmoonori-afk/birkin-mnemosyne
commit 63a34526973fc9ad0e5a030a474c67a5fca873e7
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 ashmoonori (LICENSE)

The rewrite keeps what the plugin gives a user: durable notes as Markdown under
one vault, create-only writes, ranked lexical recall with an AND label filter,
reading one note whole, and reversible archiving that previews before it moves a
file and never deletes one, plus the digest the original puts in the prompt.
The Python provider was reimplemented against Nodecode's contract: the six
provider tools became five `birkin_*` tools, the system-prompt block became a
`:round` hook, and the vault lives under the Nodecode home unless the section
names another folder. Left out, because they are Python seams Nodecode does not
have or optional extras the original disables by default: the sixth tool,
`birkin_memory_index`, which reads the original's resident index and topic
views; the MCP server and its CLI; the model-driven curation prompts and
consolidation runs; the opt-in session-transcript handoffs; and the optional
semantic-embedding and rerank legs. Scoring is the same BM25 shape without the
original's zone-decay and Hebbian access boosting, and no index or cache file
is written beside the notes: the Markdown files are the whole store.
